2. Clinical toxicology
(a)
Types of Poisons:
(i)
Corrosive poisons (Mineral acids, Caustic alkalis, Organic acids, Vegetable acids)
(ii)
Irritant poisons (Organic poisons - Vegetable and animal; Inorganic poisons - metallic and non-metallic; Mechanical
poisons)
(iii)
Asphyxiant poisons (Carbon monoxide; Carbon dioxide; Hydrogen sulphide and some war gases)
(iv)
Neurotic poisons (Opium, Nux vomica, Alcohol, Fuels like kerosene and petroleum products, Cannabis indica, Dhatura,
Anaesthetics Sedatives and Hypnotics, Agrochemical compounds, Belladonna, Hyoscyamus, Curare, Conium)
(v)
Cardiac poisons (Digitalis purpurea, Oleander, Aconite, Nicotine)
(vi)
Miscellaneous poisons (Analgesics and Antipyretics, Antihistaminics, Tranquillisers, antidepressants, Stimulants,
Hallucinogens, Street drugs etc.)
